<h2 id="homology-section-product-exact" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="060J">12.32</span> Exactness of products</h2>

<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="060K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060K">Lemma <span data-tag="060K">12.32.1</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a set. For $i \in I$ let $L_ i \to M_ i \to N_ i$ be a complex of abelian groups. Let $H_ i = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(M_ i \to N_ i)/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(L_ i \to M_ i)$ be the cohomology. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \prod L_ i \to \prod M_ i \to \prod N_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> is a complex of abelian groups with homology $\prod H_ i$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
